# Binary data files, marked explicitly.
#
# With an empty .gitattributes git falls back to `text=auto`, which means it SNIFFS each file to
# decide whether to normalise line endings. Sniffing is reliable for these (they all contain NUL
# early), so nothing has actually been corrupted — but the safety of a 22 MB SQLite database should
# not rest on a heuristic, and `git diff` wasting time generating a textual diff of a tile pack is
# its own small tax. These are also the files that dominate repository size, so being explicit about
# what they are is worth the four lines.
*.sqlite   binary
*.mbtiles  binary
*.lzpack   binary
*.zip      binary
*.p8       binary
*.pdf      binary
